api.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Feedlot API exactly as declared in contracts/openapi.yaml, with no undocumented operations or product-screen routes, including its paths, methods, parameters, schemas, status codes, and security rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined authentication, session, dashboard, and filtered lot data; support procurement imports and allocation traceability, including matching and conflict results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contract-defined lot forecasts, forecast settings, metrics, insights and actions, and weight-history operations, including their calculations, persisted updates, and specified errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contract-defined inventory reads, writes, movements, projections, and CSV exports, persisting valid inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contract-defined ration reads, creation, revision, optimization, and approval, persisting valid changes and returning calculated results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contract-defined feed-plan reads, creation, review, and status changes, including calculated quantities, audit state, and execution status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contract-defined feeding-event reads, creation, correction, and voiding, including variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, updated lot feed totals, and persistent writes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contract-defined operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports and exports, with permission-filtered rows, calculations, summaries, and requested artifacts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement sample-data reads, loading, reset, and replacement with contract-defined status and records, avoiding duplicate loads and requiring explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in the PostgreSQL database configured by the App connection string, preserve successful writes across API restarts, and upgrade existing databases to the contract schema without losing existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, run SeedData.Run at startup to add 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived sample rows to each empty application table, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing seed-write errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, serve collection operations from persisted records only, returning empty collections when no records exist.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}